  {
    "ply": 45,
    "san": "Ne4",
    "comment": "Only nervousnes\ns can explain such a mistake by Alekhine. It was necessary to defend with 23.\nRac1. Witnesses tell that right in that moment a waiter brought some coffee to\nAlekhine. He thanked the waiter and still looking at the chessboard put a\npiece of sugar in the coffee cup. Only at the last moment he realized that it\nwas not a piece of sugar but ... a white pawn. While he realized his mistake,\nhe got upset, said something, pushed the cup away and .... coffee spilled out\nof the cup. Mikenas too noticed his opponent apparent nervousness, and perhaps\ndistracted by this fact he immediately took the Knight.",
    "nags": []
  },
  {
    "ply": 46,
    "san": "Bxe4",
    "comment": "After this\nmove Mikenas realized that strangely his opponent was smiling. With a\ntrembling hand Alekhine pointed to the c2 square and said:\" Young man, if you\nplayed Rc2 you had won at once.\" Mikenas confesses: \"Only after Alekhine's\nwords I realized that I had such an opportunity.\"",
    "nags": []
